{% doc %}
  Apex bootstrap. Render once near the end of <head> in layout/theme.liquid.
  Emits the config JSON island, then loads the attribution engine and the
  cart-volume helper.

  Script order matters: apex-attribution.js defines
  window.__APEX_SYNC_CART_METAFIELDS__, which apex-cart-volume.js calls after
  cart mutations. Both are deferred, so they execute in document order and the
  global is always defined before the helper looks for it.

  Both scripts load unconditionally. Whether attribution actually runs is
  decided in JS from the config island (attribution_enabled), so the kill
  switch lives in exactly one place and a cached page can never ship without
  the scripts.

  @example
  {% render 'apex-attribution' %}
{% enddoc %}

{% render 'apex-config' %}

<script src="{{ 'apex-attribution.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'apex-cart-volume.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
